    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d250">

                <pb facs="0302" n="268" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg268"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sherman to Sir
                            Julian Pauncefote.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-04-16"><hi rendition="#italic">April 16,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 643.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have pleasure in confirming and
                    repeating the oral assurance heretofore given you, that the Government of the
                    United States will welcome the visit of Professor Thompson to the Pribilof <pb
                        facs="0303" n="269" xml:id="pg269"/> Islands, and that orders will at once
                    be issued to the authorities on the islands to extend to him the same facilities
                    granted him during his visit last year.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Sherman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
